- How would you adapt for field-level strong consistency needs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests offline-first design, deterministic scoring, and conflict handling in sync.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first workflows and local persistence
- Deterministic scoring with seeds for reproducibility
- Conflict resolution strategies (last-write-wins, vector clocks)

## Code Example
```javascript
function scoreBaseline(params, seed){
  let x = seed ^ (params.user_id_masked || '').length;
  x = (x * 1664525) >>> 0;
  const localeFactor = (params.locale || 'en').charCodeAt(0) & 0xff;
  x = (x ^ localeFactor) >>> 0;
  const versionFactor = (params.local_version || 'v1').length;
  x = (x * (versionFactor + 7)) >>> 0;
  const score = Math.abs(x) % 100;
  return score;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes understanding of secure multi-tenant design, auditable operations, and basic access control in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts

- JWT-based auth with tenant_id boundaries
- Row-Level Security or tenant-scoped data stores
- Immutable/append-only audit log with canonical fields
- Model versioning exposure and validation
- End-to-end test strategy for security and data isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo middleware to verify JWT and enforce tenant boundary
function authorize(req) {
  const token = req.headers['authorization'];
  const payload = verifyJwt(token);
  if (!payload || payload.tenant_id !== req.params.tenant_id) throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  return payload;
}
```

